A||N||7||wxxo||fuel filter location??||||1||
Z||000000||wxxo||03-12-2000||01:22 PM||||where is the fuel filter and how hard is it to change?? 86se ||||reg||1
Z||000001||la9||03-12-2000||01:43 PM||||it is about in the middle of the car at the bottom of the firewall. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||03-12-2000||01:46 PM||||It's a fun fun job.  You've gotta jack it up and under the car near the firewall on the passenger side. It's pretty easy to access from there.  Pull the fuel pump fuse, and start the car.  Let it run until it dies(should only be a few seconds.)  If you do that, you'll have a smaller mess in the end.  When you remove it, there's still going to be some spillage, but don't worry. Just make sure the new one is nice and snug, and then replace your fuel pump fuse.  To re-pressurize the system, the Haynes manual says you need to turn try starting it in like 2 second intervals until it fires up again.  It worked for me.  later...||||reg||1
Z||000003||kupop87gt||03-12-2000||05:27 PM||||Is this a 2.5L or 2.8L?<BR>There's a pressure relief valve on the V6 isn't there?||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FieroGTRacingInc||03-12-2000||08:08 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Do you still have to use the relief~valve if you pull the fuse and let it run itself out???||||reg||1
Z||000005||Patrick's Dad||03-12-2000||09:10 PM||||There is a pressure relief valve on the fuel rail of the V6. If you follow the instructions above (Pull the fuse, let it run, crank it a bit) you won't need to fuss with it.<P>If it's the Duke (4 cyl) the Fuel Filter couldn't be easier to deal with. It's located right in front of you as you look at the engine with the decklid open. It's about 1 3/4" in diameter, and almost 4" long. It's been a while since I had my four, but I believe it's strapped to the block by a single hex screw underneath the filter.<P>As noted the 6 cyl FF is beneath the seats, essentially, in the middle, just aft of the fuel tank.||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||03-12-2000||09:13 PM||||It's not necessary.  I lost about a 1/8 cup of gas when I removed my filter.... not much at all.||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FieroGTRacingInc||03-13-2000||12:43 AM||||Thank's for all the information...  ||||reg||1
